.Dd November 15, 2026
.Dt MIXER 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mixer
.Nd set the volume, mute or query the status of an audio: stream
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm volume Ar percent
.Nm
.Cm mute
.Nm
.Cm status
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
opens a control stream on
.Dv audio:out0
and applies the B40 protocol operations to it.
.Cm volume
maps 0 to 100 percent onto the Q15 left/right gain (100 percent is 32768);
.Cm mute
sets both channels to zero;
.Cm status
prints the stream position, underrun count and state.
.Pp
The operation applies to the control stream; a device-wide mixer is the HDA path (B44).
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It 0
The operation completed.
.It 1
The audio server returned an error.
.It 2
Usage error.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Dl $ mixer volume 50
.Dl mixer: volume 50% left=16384 right=16384
.Dl $ mixer status
.Dl mixer: status position=0 underruns=0 stopped
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr beep 1 ,
.Xr play 1 ,
.Xr audiod 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
utility first appeared in RavenBSD 0.1.
